      "name": "Senior Move Operations",
      "description": "Senior move operations: a senior move run end to end as one accountable job. The published sequence: a quote request (Short Quick Quote by default, or the Detailed Project form, switchable in place with the From, To and What's moving entries preserved); an optional free film-only video-walkthrough survey, using the survey room's Senior prompt set — main living areas, bedroom and personal rooms, keepsakes and fragile items, one prompt per screen; a human-made estimate (never auto-priced); one flat price agreed in writing before move day, with no hourly clock, ever; packing support, including fragile items and keepsakes; the move itself; and close-out. The survey media stays private — never published, never emailed, never shared with third-party AI — and auto-deletes 24 hours after upload. No price, discount, deposit, or special offer is stated for senior moves: the page's FAQ says so directly. Where a senior move actually involves a high-mass asset of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, that item moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation with floor deflection analysis to L/360, as part of the same flat-rate move — a conditional that applies only where such an asset is actually involved, never to senior moves as a class. The published record does not state whether every part of a senior move is performed by one provider's own supervised teams; that question is recorded as open in the research file and no claim is made either way. No crew-size or truck claim is published for senior moves.",
